/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 2 Kings chapters 6-10
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("2kings", [
{n:6, name:"The Iron That Swam", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 6:16",verse:"And he answered, Fear not: for they that be with us are more than they that be with them."}, facts:["Did you know the floating axe head is one of Elisha's quietest miracles? A borrowed tool, lost in the Jordan, floated back up when Elisha cast in a stick (2 Kings 6:6).","Did you know Elisha knew the Syrian king's war plans word for word, even what he spoke in his bedchamber? His servant said, 'Elisha, the prophet that is in Israel, telleth the king of Israel the words that thou speakest in thy bedchamber' (2 Kings 6:12).","Did you know Elisha prayed about eyesight twice in one day? First he asked God to open his servant's eyes to the chariots of fire, then he asked God to shut the Syrians' eyes in blindness (2 Kings 6:17-18)."], questions:[
{q:"Why did the sons of the prophets say their dwelling place was a problem?", options:["It was too strait for them","It was too far from the Jordan","It had no well","It was haunted by Syrians"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:1",verse:"And the sons of the prophets said unto Elisha, Behold now, the place where we dwell with thee is too strait for us.", insight:"God's people outgrow tight places; healthy growth always needs more room."},
{q:"What did the sons of the prophets propose to do at the Jordan?", options:["Take every man a beam and build a place to dwell","Build a temple to the LORD","Dig a new well","Cross over to escape Syria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:2",verse:"Let us go, we pray thee, unto Jordan, and take thence every man a beam, and let us make us a place there, where we may dwell. And he answered, Go ye.", insight:"They brought their need to Elisha first; plans formed with God's counsel stand."},
{q:"What happened while one of them was felling a beam?", options:["The axe head fell into the water","The beam crushed his hand","The tree fell on their camp","His axe handle broke in two"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:5",verse:"But as one was felling a beam, the axe head fell into the water: and he cried, and said, Alas, master! for it was borrowed.", insight:"Honest work can still meet sudden loss; trouble finds even the diligent."},
{q:"Why did the lost axe head matter so much to the man?", options:["It was borrowed","It belonged to the king","It was made of gold","It was his only weapon"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:5",verse:"But as one was felling a beam, the axe head fell into the water: and he cried, and said, Alas, master! for it was borrowed.", insight:"Borrowed things weigh heavier; integrity grieves over what is not ours."},
{q:"How did Elisha recover the sunken axe head?", options:["He cut down a stick, cast it in, and the iron did swim","He prayed and the river parted","He sent divers to search the deep","He commanded a fish to bring it up"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:6",verse:"And the man of God said, Where fell it? And he shewed him the place. And he cut down a stick, and cast it in thither; and the iron did swim.", insight:"God bends nature to care for small losses; nothing you truly need is beneath His notice."},
{q:"What did Elisha say when the iron floated up?", options:["Take it up to thee","Leave it for the poor","Melt it into nails","Give it to the king"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:7",verse:"Therefore said he, Take it up to thee. And he put out his hand, and took it.", insight:"Miracles are meant to be received; stretch out your hand and take what God restores."},
{q:"What was the king of Syria doing against Israel?", options:["Taking counsel with his servants where his camp would be","Sending tribute to the king of Israel","Building a fortress at Dothan","Withdrawing his armies home"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:8",verse:"Then the king of Syria warred against Israel, and took counsel with his servants, saying, In such and such a place shall be my camp.", insight:"Wicked plans are made in council rooms, but God hears every one."},
{q:"What warning did Elisha send the king of Israel?", options:["Beware that thou pass not such a place, for the Syrians are come down","Attack the Syrians at midnight","Flee the land of Israel","Surrender Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:9",verse:"And the man of God sent unto the king of Israel, saying, Beware that thou pass not such a place; for thither the Syrians are come down.", insight:"God warns before He delivers; heed the warning and the danger passes you by."},
{q:"How many times did Elisha's warnings save the king?", options:["Not once nor twice","Only a single time","Exactly seven times","Never, the king ignored him"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:10",verse:"And the king of Israel sent to the place which the man of God told him and warned him of, and saved himself there, not once nor twice.", insight:"God repeats His rescues; His patience outlasts our peril."},
{q:"How did a Syrian servant explain the leaked war plans?", options:["Elisha tells the king of Israel the words spoken in the king's bedchamber","A spy among the Syrians betrayed them","The Israelites bribed the cooks","A traitor sold the maps"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:12",verse:"And one of his servants said, None, my lord, O king: but Elisha, the prophet that is in Israel, telleth the king of Israel the words that thou speakest in thy bedchamber.", insight:"No secret is safe from God; He hears what is whispered behind closed doors."},
{q:"Where did the Syrians learn Elisha was?", options:["In Dothan","In Damascus","In Samaria","In Bethel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:13",verse:"And he said, Go and spy where he is, that I may send and fetch him. And it was told him, saying, Behold, he is in Dothan.", insight:"Dothan, a small place, would host one of Scripture's great visions."},
{q:"What force came by night to seize Elisha?", options:["Horses, chariots, and a great host","A single assassin","A band of spies","A plague of darkness"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:14",verse:"Therefore sent he thither horses, and chariots, and a great host: and they came by night, and compassed the city about.", insight:"The enemy sends armies against one man of God; heaven counts one prayerful man a match for them."},
{q:"What did Elisha's servant cry when he saw the army?", options:["Alas, my master! how shall we do?","The LORD has delivered them","Let us surrender at once","Sound the alarm in Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:15",verse:"And when the servant of the man of God was risen early, and gone forth, behold, an host compassed the city both with horses and chariots. And his servant said unto him, Alas, my master! how shall we do?", insight:"Fear speaks first and loudest; faith answers it with better news."},
{q:"How did Elisha answer his servant's fear?", options:["Fear not: for they that be with us are more than they that be with them","We must flee to Egypt","Pray that we die quickly","Hide, and I will fight alone"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:16",verse:"And he answered, Fear not: for they that be with us are more than they that be with them.", insight:"Count heaven's host before you count the enemy's; the unseen army is the larger one."},
{q:"What did the servant see when his eyes were opened?", options:["The mountain full of horses and chariots of fire round about Elisha","An angel standing with a drawn sword","The Syrian army turning to flee","A cloud descending on Dothan"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:17",verse:"And Elisha prayed, and said, LORD, I pray thee, open his eyes, that he may see. And the LORD opened the eyes of the young man; and he saw: and, behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire round about Elisha.", insight:"Prayer opened eyes, not heavens; the help was already there, waiting to be seen."},
{q:"What did Elisha pray over the Syrian army?", options:["Smite this people with blindness","Rain fire from heaven","Turn their swords on each other","Paralyze their horses"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:18",verse:"And when they came down to him, Elisha prayed unto the LORD, and said, Smite this people, I pray thee, with blindness. And he smote them with blindness according to the word of Elisha.", insight:"Blindness, not death; God disarms enemies He means to feed."},
{q:"Where did Elisha lead the blinded Syrians?", options:["To Samaria","To Damascus","To the river Jordan","Back to Dothan"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:19",verse:"And Elisha said unto them, This is not the way, neither is this the city: follow me, and I will bring you to the man whom ye seek. But he led them to Samaria.", insight:"He promised to bring them to the man they sought, and did; truth can be kind and clever at once."},
{q:"How did Elisha say the captives should be treated?", options:["Set bread and water before them, and send them to their master","Smite them with the sword","Sell them as slaves","Imprison them in Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:22",verse:"And he answered, Thou shalt not smite them: wouldest thou smite those whom thou hast taken captive with thy sword and with thy bow? set bread and water before them, that they may eat and drink, and go to their master.", insight:"Feed your captured enemies; grace at the table does what swords cannot."},
{q:"How desperate was the famine in besieged Samaria?", options:["An ass's head sold for fourscore pieces of silver, and dove's dung for five","Bread sold for a shekel a loaf","The people ate grass from the walls","Water cost more than gold"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:25",verse:"And there was a great famine in Samaria: and, behold, they besieged it, until an ass’s head was sold for fourscore pieces of silver, and the fourth part of a cab of dove’s dung for five pieces of silver.", insight:"Siege hunger cheapens everything except food; famine exposes what we truly trust."},
{q:"What did the king of Israel swear when the famine grew desperate?", options:["That Elisha's head would not stand on him that day","That he would surrender to Syria","That he would tear down the temple","That he would flee to Judah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 6:31",verse:"Then he said, God do so and more also to me, if the head of Elisha the son of Shaphat shall stand on him this day.", insight:"Desperate men blame God's messengers; the king's oath exposed his heart."}
]},
{n:7, name:"The Siege Lifted", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 7:1",verse:"Then Elisha said, Hear ye the word of the LORD; Thus saith the LORD, To morrow about this time shall a measure of fine flour be sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria."}, facts:["Did you know Elisha's prophecy named both the price and the place? A measure of fine flour for a shekel, two measures of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria, by tomorrow about this time (2 Kings 7:1).","Did you know the four lepers became Samaria's first evangelists? They said, 'This day is a day of good tidings, and we hold our peace,' and carried the news to the starving city (2 Kings 7:9).","Did you know the Syrians' panic left a trail all the way to the Jordan? The scouts found the whole road full of garments and vessels they had cast away in their haste (2 Kings 7:15)."], questions:[
{q:"What did Elisha promise would happen about this time tomorrow?", options:["A measure of fine flour for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel","The Syrians would surrender","Rain would fall on Samaria","The king would die"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:1",verse:"Then Elisha said, Hear ye the word of the LORD; Thus saith the LORD, To morrow about this time shall a measure of fine flour be sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria.", insight:"God sets a time on His mercy; tomorrow about this time, plenty returns."},
{q:"How was Elisha's word about the flour fulfilled?", options:["The people spoiled the Syrian tents, and flour sold for a shekel as promised","The Syrians returned to besiege again","The king shut the city gates","The lepers kept the spoil for themselves"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:16",verse:"And the people went out, and spoiled the tents of the Syrians. So a measure of fine flour was sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, according to the word of the LORD.", insight:"To the very shekel, the word held; God's promises keep exact accounts."},
{q:"Who doubted Elisha's word?", options:["A lord on whose hand the king leaned","The king of Israel himself","Gehazi the servant","The captain of the guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:2",verse:"Then a lord on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God, and said, Behold, if the LORD would make windows in heaven, might this thing be? And he said, Behold, thou shalt see it with thine eyes, but shalt not eat thereof.", insight:"Proximity to power does not produce faith; the man nearest the king was farthest from belief."},
{q:"How did the lord mock the promise?", options:["Behold, if the LORD would make windows in heaven, might this thing be?","The prophet dreams while we starve","Let God send manna as in the wilderness","This is the famine talking"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:2",verse:"Then a lord on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God, and said, Behold, if the LORD would make windows in heaven, might this thing be? And he said, Behold, thou shalt see it with thine eyes, but shalt not eat thereof.", insight:"Mockery dresses unbelief as reason; 'windows in heaven' admits God is big but denies He cares."},
{q:"What did Elisha tell the doubting lord?", options:["Thou shalt see it with thine eyes, but shalt not eat thereof","Thou shalt be hanged at the gate","Thy house shall be cursed forever","Thou shalt be struck blind"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:19",verse:"And that lord answered the man of God, and said, Now, behold, if the LORD should make windows in heaven, might such a thing be? And he said, Behold, thou shalt see it with thine eyes, but shalt not eat thereof.", insight:"Seeing without tasting is the portion of unbelief; faith feasts where doubt only watches."},
{q:"How many leprous men sat at the entering of the gate?", options:["Four","Seven","Two","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:3",verse:"And there were four leprous men at the entering in of the gate: and they said one to another, Why sit we here until we die?", insight:"Four outcasts at the gate would carry Samaria's salvation; God uses the despised."},
{q:"What question moved the lepers to act?", options:["Why sit we here until we die?","Who will feed us tomorrow?","Where is the prophet?","When will the siege end?"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:3",verse:"And there were four leprous men at the entering in of the gate: and they said one to another, Why sit we here until we die?", insight:"'Why sit we here until we die?' Despair can be the doorway to daring."},
{q:"When did the lepers rise to go to the Syrian camp?", options:["In the twilight","At midnight","At the dawn","At noon"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:5",verse:"And they rose up in the twilight, to go unto the camp of the Syrians: and when they were come to the uttermost part of the camp of Syria, behold, there was no man there.", insight:"They walked into the dusk not knowing God had already emptied the camp."},
{q:"What did the lepers find at the Syrian camp?", options:["No man there","A great feast prepared","The Syrian king waiting","Guards asleep at their posts"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:5",verse:"And they rose up in the twilight, to go unto the camp of the Syrians: and when they were come to the uttermost part of the camp of Syria, behold, there was no man there.", insight:"The camp stood empty; God had fought the battle while Samaria slept."},
{q:"What had the Lord made the Syrians hear?", options:["A noise of chariots, horses, and a great host","Thunder from a clear sky","Elisha praying on the mountain","The walls of Samaria falling"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:6",verse:"For the Lord had made the host of the Syrians to hear a noise of chariots, and a noise of horses, even the noise of a great host: and they said one to another, Lo, the king of Israel hath hired against us the kings of the Hittites, and the kings of the Egyptians, to come upon us.", insight:"A sound routed an army; God needs no sword when fear will do."},
{q:"What did the Syrians conclude about the noise?", options:["The king of Israel had hired the Hittites and the Egyptians against them","The gods of Israel were angry","An earthquake was coming","Their own allies had betrayed them"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:6",verse:"For the Lord had made the host of the Syrians to hear a noise of chariots, and a noise of horses, even the noise of a great host: and they said one to another, Lo, the king of Israel hath hired against us the kings of the Hittites, and the kings of the Egyptians, to come upon us.", insight:"God let them imagine the worst; terror invents its own enemies."},
{q:"What did the fleeing Syrians leave behind?", options:["Their tents, horses, and asses, even the camp as it was","Only their weapons","Burning fires","Their wounded soldiers"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:7",verse:"Wherefore they arose and fled in the twilight, and left their tents, and their horses, and their asses, even the camp as it was, and fled for their life.", insight:"They fled for their life and left their livelihood; panic abandons what patience would have kept."},
{q:"What did the lepers do in the empty tents?", options:["Ate and drank, and hid silver, gold, and raiment","Set the camp on fire","Freed the prisoners","Gathered weapons for Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:8",verse:"And when these lepers came to the uttermost part of the camp, they went into one tent, and did eat and drink, and carried thence silver, and gold, and raiment, and went and hid it; and came again, and entered into another tent, and carried thence also, and went and hid it.", insight:"First they feasted, then they hoarded; blessing turns to guilt when it is hidden."},
{q:"What convicted the lepers about hiding the spoil?", options:["This is a day of good tidings, and we hold our peace","The king will punish us","The Syrians may return","Our fellow lepers are starving"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:9",verse:"Then they said one to another, We do not well: this day is a day of good tidings, and we hold our peace: if we tarry till the morning light, some mischief will come upon us: now therefore come, that we may go and tell the king’s household.", insight:"Good news hoarded becomes guilt; the lepers became Samaria's first evangelists."},
{q:"Whom did the lepers tell first?", options:["The porter of the city","The king himself","Elisha the prophet","The captain of the guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:10",verse:"So they came and called unto the porter of the city: and they told them, saying, We came to the camp of the Syrians, and, behold, there was no man there, neither voice of man, but horses tied, and asses tied, and the tents as they were.", insight:"They told the porter, the lowest watchman; good tidings climb from the bottom up."},
{q:"What did the king fear the Syrians had done?", options:["Hidden in the field to catch Israel alive and get into the city","Poisoned the wells","Burned their own camp to deceive","Fled back to Damascus for good"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:12",verse:"And the king arose in the night, and said unto his servants, I will now shew you what the Syrians have done to us. They know that we be hungry; therefore are they gone out of the camp to hide themselves in the field, saying, When they come out of the city, we shall catch them alive, and get into the city.", insight:"Suspicion almost starved the city; a fearful heart doubts even deliverance."},
{q:"How did the king test whether the camp was truly empty?", options:["He sent two chariot horses to go and see","He sent a hundred soldiers","He waited three days","He asked Elisha for a sign"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:14",verse:"They took therefore two chariot horses; and the king sent after the host of the Syrians, saying, Go and see.", insight:"'Go and see'; some will only believe what scouts confirm."},
{q:"What did the messengers find on the way to Jordan?", options:["Garments and vessels the Syrians had cast away in their haste","The Syrian army regrouping","A second abandoned city","The lepers' hidden treasure"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:15",verse:"And they went after them unto Jordan: and, lo, all the way was full of garments and vessels, which the Syrians had cast away in their haste. And the messengers returned, and told the king.", insight:"The road was littered with panic; haste leaves a trail."},
{q:"What did the people do when they heard?", options:["They went out and spoiled the tents of the Syrians","They shut the gates tighter","They offered sacrifices first","They marched on Damascus"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:16",verse:"And the people went out, and spoiled the tents of the Syrians. So a measure of fine flour was sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, according to the word of the LORD.", insight:"The hungry became the harvesters; God's word turned a siege into a spoil."},
{q:"What happened to the lord who had doubted?", options:["The people trode upon him in the gate, and he died","He was hanged by the king","He fled to the Syrians","He became a leper"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 7:20",verse:"And so it fell out unto him: for the people trode upon him in the gate, and he died.", insight:"He saw the plenty and never tasted it; unbelief gets a front-row seat to blessings it cannot share."}
]},
{n:8, name:"Elisha Weeps for Israel", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 8:19",verse:"Yet the LORD would not destroy Judah for David his servant’s sake, as he promised him to give him alway a light, and to his children."}, facts:["Did you know the Shunammite woman got back more than she lost? The king restored her land and all the fruits of the field since the day she left, seven years of harvests (2 Kings 8:6).","Did you know Hazael came to Elisha with forty camels loaded with every good thing of Damascus? Royal gifts could not buy the answer he feared (2 Kings 8:9).","Did you know Elisha wept while staring at the man who would be king? He saw the evil Hazael would do to Israel and could not hold back his tears (2 Kings 8:11-12)."], questions:[
{q:"What did Elisha tell the Shunammite woman to do?", options:["Arise, and sojourn wheresoever thou canst, for the LORD hath called for a famine","Flee to Egypt at once","Hide her son in the hills","Build a house in Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:1",verse:"Then spake Elisha unto the woman, whose son he had restored to life, saying, Arise, and go thou and thine household, and sojourn wheresoever thou canst sojourn: for the LORD hath called for a famine; and it shall also come upon the land seven years.", insight:"God warns His own before judgment falls; the prophet's word was her protection."},
{q:"How long would the famine last?", options:["Seven years","Three years","Forty days","One year"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:1",verse:"Then spake Elisha unto the woman, whose son he had restored to life, saying, Arise, and go thou and thine household, and sojourn wheresoever thou canst sojourn: for the LORD hath called for a famine; and it shall also come upon the land seven years.", insight:"Seven years, the full measure; God's warnings are specific because His care is."},
{q:"What is recorded of Jehoram when he began to reign over Judah?", options:["Thirty and two years old was he, and he reigned eight years in Jerusalem","Two and twenty years old was he, and he reigned one year","Forty years old was he, and he reigned twelve years","Eighteen years old was he, and he reigned forty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:17",verse:"Thirty and two years old was he when he began to reign; and he reigned eight years in Jerusalem.", insight:"Thirty-two and eight years; a short reign with a long shadow."},
{q:"What did the woman return to cry for?", options:["Her house and her land","Her stolen cattle","Her husband's debts","Her son's inheritance"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:3",verse:"And it came to pass at the seven years’ end, that the woman returned out of the land of the Philistines: and she went forth to cry unto the king for her house and for her land.", insight:"She cried to the king for her house and land; heaven had already arranged the hearing."},
{q:"Whom was the king talking with when the woman arrived?", options:["Gehazi the servant of the man of God","The captain of his guard","The high priest","The queen mother"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:4",verse:"And the king talked with Gehazi the servant of the man of God, saying, Tell me, I pray thee, all the great things that Elisha hath done.", insight:"The king was hearing Elisha's stories at the very moment the story walked in."},
{q:"What was Gehazi telling the king when the woman arrived?", options:["How Elisha had restored a dead body to life, and behold, this was the very woman and her son","How the axe head had swum in the Jordan","How the Syrians had been blinded at Dothan","How Naaman had been cleansed of leprosy"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:5",verse:"And it came to pass, as he was telling the king how he had restored a dead body to life, that, behold, the woman, whose son he had restored to life, cried to the king for her house and for her land. And Gehazi said, My lord, O king, this is the woman, and this is her son, whom Elisha restored to life.", insight:"The witness became the evidence; God times testimonies to the moment of need."},
{q:"How old was Ahaziah when he began to reign, and who was his mother?", options:["Two and twenty, and his mother was Athaliah the daughter of Omri","Thirty and two, and his mother was Jezebel","Eighteen, and his mother was a daughter of David","Forty, and his mother is not named"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:26",verse:"Two and twenty years old was Ahaziah when he began to reign; and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Athaliah, the daughter of Omri king of Israel.", insight:"Twenty-two, one year, Athaliah's son; Ahab's blood ran in Judah's throne."},
{q:"What did the king command for the woman?", options:["Restore all that was hers, and all the fruits of the field since she left","Give her a house in Jerusalem","Pay her a thousand shekels","Make her a servant in the palace"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:6",verse:"And when the king asked the woman, she told him. So the king appointed unto her a certain officer, saying, Restore all that was hers, and all the fruits of the field since the day that she left the land, even until now.", insight:"Not just her land, but seven years of harvests; God repays what obedience cost."},
{q:"Where did Elisha go after this?", options:["To Damascus","To Samaria","To Bethel","To Jericho"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:7",verse:"And Elisha came to Damascus; and Ben-hadad the king of Syria was sick; and it was told him, saying, The man of God is come hither.", insight:"The man of God walked into the enemy's capital; God's servants go where they are needed, not where they are safe."},
{q:"Who was sick in Damascus?", options:["Ben-hadad king of Syria","Hazael his servant","The queen of Syria","Naaman the captain"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:7",verse:"And Elisha came to Damascus; and Ben-hadad the king of Syria was sick; and it was told him, saying, The man of God is come hither.", insight:"A sick king sent for the prophet of his enemy; trouble makes strange seekers."},
{q:"Whom did Ben-hadad send to Elisha?", options:["Hazael","His eldest son","The captain of his guard","A company of priests"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:8",verse:"And the king said unto Hazael, Take a present in thine hand, and go, meet the man of God, and enquire of the LORD by him, saying, Shall I recover of this disease?", insight:"He sent Hazael, the very man who would take his throne; God was already arranging the succession."},
{q:"What present did Hazael bring?", options:["Every good thing of Damascus, forty camels' burden","Gold from the temple","A hundred horses","The crown jewels of Syria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:9",verse:"So Hazael went to meet him, and took a present with him, even of every good thing of Damascus, forty camels’ burden, and came and stood before him, and said, Thy son Ben-hadad king of Syria hath sent me to thee, saying, Shall I recover of this disease?", insight:"Forty camels of gifts; kings try to buy what only God can give."},
{q:"In whose days did Edom revolt from under the hand of Judah?", options:["In the days of Jehoram","In the days of Jehoshaphat","In the days of Ahaziah","In the days of Elisha"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:20",verse:"In his days Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah, and made a king over themselves.", insight:"Edom broke away; sin in the palace costs strength on the borders."},
{q:"What answer did Elisha send back?", options:["Thou mayest certainly recover, but the LORD hath shewed me that he shall surely die","Thou shalt surely die of this disease","Go in peace, for thou art healed","The LORD will not answer thee"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:10",verse:"And Elisha said unto him, Go, say unto him, Thou mayest certainly recover: howbeit the LORD hath shewed me that he shall surely die.", insight:"Recover, yet die; the disease would not kill him, but the man beside him would."},
{q:"What did Elisha do as he stared at Hazael?", options:["He settled his countenance stedfastly, until he was ashamed, and the man of God wept","He laughed at the folly of kings","He turned his face to the wall","He fell down and worshipped"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:11",verse:"And he settled his countenance stedfastly, until he was ashamed: and the man of God wept.", insight:"The prophet wept before the future king; tears are the truest prophecy of coming sorrow."},
{q:"Why did Elisha weep?", options:["Because of the evil Hazael would do to the children of Israel","Because Ben-hadad would die","Because Syria would fall to Assyria","Because his own death was near"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:12",verse:"And Hazael said, Why weepeth my lord? And he answered, Because I know the evil that thou wilt do unto the children of Israel: their strong holds wilt thou set on fire, and their young men wilt thou slay with the sword, and wilt dash their children, and rip up their women with child.", insight:"He saw burned strongholds and slain young men; a prophet's tears are Israel's truest mourning."},
{q:"How did Hazael answer the prophecy of his cruelty?", options:["But what, is thy servant a dog, that he should do this great thing?","I will do even worse to Israel","The prophet lies about me","I am not worthy of such power"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:13",verse:"And Hazael said, But what, is thy servant a dog, that he should do this great thing? And Elisha answered, The LORD hath shewed me that thou shalt be king over Syria.", insight:"'Is thy servant a dog?' Men deny the evil they are already capable of."},
{q:"What did Elisha reveal to Hazael?", options:["The LORD hath shewed me that thou shalt be king over Syria","Thou shalt die within a year","Thy sons shall serve Israel","Syria shall fall to thee in war"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:13",verse:"And Hazael said, But what, is thy servant a dog, that he should do this great thing? And Elisha answered, The LORD hath shewed me that thou shalt be king over Syria.", insight:"A word of destiny to a murderer; God raises up even cruel kings for His purposes."},
{q:"What did Hazael tell Ben-hadad?", options:["He told me that thou shouldest surely recover","Elisha refused to answer","The prophet cursed thee","Thou shalt die within a month"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:14",verse:"So he departed from Elisha, and came to his master; who said to him, What said Elisha to thee? And he answered, He told me that thou shouldest surely recover.", insight:"He reported the comforting half and hid the rest; half-truths serve murderers well."},
{q:"How did Ben-hadad die the next morning?", options:["Hazael spread a thick cloth dipped in water on his face","He died of his disease in his sleep","He was stabbed by his guards","He fell from his chariot"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 8:15",verse:"And it came to pass on the morrow, that he took a thick cloth, and dipped it in water, and spread it on his face, so that he died: and Hazael reigned in his stead.", insight:"A wet cloth, not a sword; the cruelest deaths are sometimes the quietest."}
]},
{n:9, name:"Jehu Is Anointed", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 9:37",verse:"And the carcase of Jezebel shall be as dung upon the face of the field in the portion of Jezreel; so that they shall not say, This is Jezebel."}, facts:["Did you know Jehu was anointed with a simple box of oil in an inner chamber, and the young prophet was told to open the door and flee? No crown, no crowd, just oil and a word (2 Kings 9:3).","Did you know Jehu drove so furiously that his own watchman recognized him by it? 'The driving is like the driving of Jehu the son of Nimshi; for he driveth furiously' (2 Kings 9:20).","Did you know dogs left almost nothing of Jezebel? When they went to bury her, they found no more than the skull, the feet, and the palms of her hands (2 Kings 9:35)."], questions:[
{q:"Whom did Elisha send to anoint the new king?", options:["One of the children of the prophets","Gehazi his servant","A captain of Israel","An elder of Ramoth-gilead"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:1",verse:"And Elisha the prophet called one of the children of the prophets, and said unto him, Gird up thy loins, and take this box of oil in thine hand, and go to Ramoth-gilead:", insight:"A nameless young prophet carried Israel's future in a box of oil."},
{q:"What was he to take, and where was he sent?", options:["This box of oil, to Ramoth-gilead","A crown of gold, to Jezreel","A letter from Elisha, to Samaria","A sword of judgment, to Damascus"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:1",verse:"And Elisha the prophet called one of the children of the prophets, and said unto him, Gird up thy loins, and take this box of oil in thine hand, and go to Ramoth-gilead:", insight:"A box of oil, not a sword; God's anointing precedes man's fighting."},
{q:"Whom was he to anoint, and where?", options:["Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi, in an inner chamber","Joram the son of Ahab, in the palace","Ahaziah king of Judah, in the temple","Hazael king of Syria, in the camp"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:2",verse:"And when thou comest thither, look out there Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi, and go in, and make him arise up from among his brethren, and carry him to an inner chamber;", insight:"Jehu, a captain, not a prince; God picks His instruments from unexpected ranks."},
{q:"What was he to do after pouring the oil on Jehu's head?", options:["Open the door, and flee, and tarry not","Stay and crown him publicly","Sound the trumpet","Bring him to Elisha"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:3",verse:"Then take the box of oil, and pour it on his head, and say, Thus saith the LORD, I have anointed thee king over Israel. Then open the door, and flee, and tarry not.", insight:"Anoint and run; God's work does not need the prophet to manage the aftermath."},
{q:"What did Jehu's fellow captains call the young prophet?", options:["This mad fellow","A holy man of God","A Syrian spy","A bearer of good news"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:11",verse:"Then Jehu came forth to the servants of his lord: and one said unto him, Is all well? wherefore came this mad fellow to thee? And he said unto them, Ye know the man, and his communication.", insight:"The world calls God's messengers mad; heaven calls them punctual."},
{q:"What did the captains do when Jehu told them the word?", options:["They put their garments under him on the top of the stairs and blew trumpets, saying, Jehu is king","They arrested him for treason","They fled to Joram","They laughed him to scorn"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:13",verse:"Then they hasted, and took every man his garment, and put it under him on the top of the stairs, and blew with trumpets, saying, Jehu is king.", insight:"Garments for a throne, trumpets for a crown; loyalty turns in an instant when God moves."},
{q:"Where did Jehu ride to confront Joram?", options:["To Jezreel, where Joram lay being healed","To Samaria","To Ramoth-gilead","To Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:16",verse:"So Jehu rode in a chariot, and went to Jezreel; for Joram lay there. And Ahaziah king of Judah was come down to see Joram.", insight:"Jezreel, where the wounded king rested; judgment finds men in their sickbeds."},
{q:"What did Jehu answer the king's messengers?", options:["What hast thou to do with peace? turn thee behind me","Peace be with thee, return to the king","I come in peace from the army","Tell the king I bring good news"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:18",verse:"So there went one on horseback to meet him, and said, Thus saith the king, Is it peace? And Jehu said, What hast thou to do with peace? turn thee behind me. And the watchman told, saying, The messenger came to them, but he cometh not again.", insight:"'What hast thou to do with peace?' Some missions have no room for negotiation."},
{q:"How did the watchman describe Jehu's driving?", options:["He driveth furiously","He rides like a king","He comes slowly and surely","He drives a chariot of fire"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:20",verse:"And the watchman told, saying, He came even unto them, and cometh not again: and the driving is like the driving of Jehu the son of Nimshi; for he driveth furiously.", insight:"Furious driving; zeal has a pace, and Jehu's was unmistakable."},
{q:"Where did Joram and Ahaziah meet Jehu?", options:["In the portion of Naboth the Jezreelite","At the gate of Jezreel","In the king's palace","On the road to Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:21",verse:"And Joram said, Make ready. And his chariot was made ready. And Joram king of Israel and Ahaziah king of Judah went out, each in his chariot, and they went out against Jehu, and met him in the portion of Naboth the Jezreelite.", insight:"Naboth's field, where Ahab's guilt was sown; judgment returns to the scene of the crime."},
{q:"How did Jehu answer Joram's question, 'Is it peace?'", options:["What peace, so long as the whoredoms of thy mother Jezebel and her witchcrafts are so many?","Peace, if thou wilt repent","There is peace between us","Ask thy mother, not me"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:22",verse:"And it came to pass, when Joram saw Jehu, that he said, Is it peace, Jehu? And he answered, What peace, so long as the whoredoms of thy mother Jezebel and her witchcrafts are so many?", insight:"No peace with unrepented evil; Jehu named the sin before he drew the bow."},
{q:"What did Joram cry to Ahaziah?", options:["There is treachery, O Ahaziah","Flee to Samaria","Fight for thy life","Surrender to Jehu"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:23",verse:"And Joram turned his hands, and fled, and said to Ahaziah, There is treachery, O Ahaziah.", insight:"Treachery, he called it; but it was justice, long delayed."},
{q:"How did Jehu kill Joram?", options:["He smote him between his arms with an arrow, and it went out at his heart","He ran him through with a spear","He had him beheaded","He threw him from his chariot"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:24",verse:"And Jehu drew a bow with his full strength, and smote Jehoram between his arms, and the arrow went out at his heart, and he sunk down in his chariot.", insight:"Between the arms, out at the heart; judgment found the center of the man."},
{q:"Where did Jehu command Joram's body to be cast?", options:["In the portion of the field of Naboth the Jezreelite","In the king's sepulchre","In the river Kishon","Outside the walls of Jezreel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:25",verse:"Then said Jehu to Bidkar his captain, Take up, and cast him in the portion of the field of Naboth the Jezreelite: for remember how that, when I and thou rode together after Ahab his father, the LORD laid this burden upon him;", insight:"Naboth's field received Ahab's son; God keeps His appointments with justice."},
{q:"Why was Joram cast into Naboth's field?", options:["The LORD had seen the blood of Naboth and his sons, and would requite Joram in that plat","It was the nearest burial ground","Jehu owned the land","The dogs were waiting there"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:26",verse:"Surely I have seen yesterday the blood of Naboth, and the blood of his sons, saith the LORD; and I will requite thee in this plat, saith the LORD. Now therefore take and cast him into the plat of ground, according to the word of the LORD.", insight:"Yesterday's blood, today's reckoning; God never forgets an unpaid debt of justice."},
{q:"How did Ahaziah king of Judah die?", options:["He was smitten at the going up to Gur by Ibleam, fled to Megiddo, and died there","He fell from his chariot at Jezreel","He was slain in his palace","He drowned in the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:27",verse:"But when Ahaziah the king of Judah saw this, he fled by the way of the garden house. And Jehu followed after him, and said, Smite him also in the chariot. And they did so at the going up to Gur, which is by Ibleam. And he fled to Megiddo, and died there.", insight:"A visiting king caught in another kingdom's judgment; alliances with evil are never safe."},
{q:"What did Jezebel do when she heard Jehu was coming?", options:["She painted her face, tired her head, and looked out at a window","She fled to the temple","She dressed in sackcloth","She sent gifts to Jehu"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:30",verse:"And when Jehu was come to Jezreel, Jezebel heard of it; and she painted her face, and tired her head, and looked out at a window.", insight:"Paint and a window; pride dresses up even for its own downfall."},
{q:"What did Jezebel say to Jehu?", options:["Had Zimri peace, who slew his master?","Welcome, king of Israel","Spare me, and I will serve thee","The gods will avenge me"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:31",verse:"And as Jehu entered in at the gate, she said, Had Zimri peace, who slew his master?", insight:"She greeted judgment with a taunt; defiance to the end is still defiance."},
{q:"What did Jehu command concerning Jezebel?", options:["Throw her down","Bring her to me alive","Spare the king's daughter","Stone her at the gate"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:33",verse:"And he said, Throw her down. So they threw her down: and some of her blood was sprinkled on the wall, and on the horses: and he trode her under foot.", insight:"'Throw her down'; the eunuchs obeyed, and pride fell from its window."},
{q:"What fulfilled Elijah's word about Jezebel?", options:["Dogs ate her in the portion of Jezreel, leaving only the skull, the feet, and the palms of her hands","She was buried with the kings","She escaped to Sidon","She repented at the last"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 9:36",verse:"Wherefore they came again, and told him. And he said, This is the word of the LORD, which he spake by his servant Elijah the Tishbite, saying, In the portion of Jezreel shall dogs eat the flesh of Jezebel:", insight:"Only skull, feet, and palms remained; God's word outlasts every queen."}
]},
{n:10, name:"Jehu Destroys Baal", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 10:28",verse:"Thus Jehu destroyed Baal out of Israel."}, facts:["Did you know Jehu stacked the heads of Ahab's seventy sons in two heaps at the gate of Jezreel and left them there until morning? The whole city saw the end of the dynasty (2 Kings 10:8).","Did you know God promised Jehu that his children to the fourth generation would sit on Israel's throne, because he executed judgment on the house of Ahab (2 Kings 10:30)?","Did you know the house of Baal ended as a draught house? Jehu's men brake down the image and the temple, and turned it into a public latrine (2 Kings 10:27)."], questions:[
{q:"How many sons did Ahab have in Samaria?", options:["Seventy","Twelve","Forty","Thirty"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:1",verse:"And Ahab had seventy sons in Samaria. And Jehu wrote letters, and sent to Samaria, unto the rulers of Jezreel, to the elders, and to them that brought up Ahab’s children, saying,", insight:"Seventy sons, a dynasty in numbers; numbers mean nothing against God's decree."},
{q:"To whom did Jehu write his challenge?", options:["The rulers of Jezreel, the elders, and them that brought up Ahab's children","The priests of Baal","The king of Judah","The captains of the army"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:1",verse:"And Ahab had seventy sons in Samaria. And Jehu wrote letters, and sent to Samaria, unto the rulers of Jezreel, to the elders, and to them that brought up Ahab’s children, saying,", insight:"He wrote to the guardians of Ahab's house; their courage would decide the day."},
{q:"What did Jehu's first letter demand?", options:["Look out the best of your master's sons, set him on his father's throne, and fight for your master's house","Surrender the city at once","Send tribute to Jezreel","Put the princes in chains"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:3",verse:"Look even out the best and meetest of your master’s sons, and set him on his father’s throne, and fight for your master’s house.", insight:"A dare, not a battle; Jehu tested their will before he tested their strength."},
{q:"How did Ahab's guardians answer?", options:["Behold, two kings stood not before him: how then shall we stand?","We will fight to the last man","We choose the eldest son","We appeal to the king of Judah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:4",verse:"But they were exceedingly afraid, and said, Behold, two kings stood not before him: how then shall we stand?", insight:"Fear answered for them; when courage fails, surrender writes itself."},
{q:"What did they send back to Jehu?", options:["We are thy servants, and will do all that thou shalt bid us; we will not make any king","We will crown the youngest prince","Come and take the city thyself","We need three days to decide"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:5",verse:"And he that was over the house, and he that was over the city, the elders also, and the bringers up of the children, sent to Jehu, saying, We are thy servants, and will do all that thou shalt bid us; we will not make any king: do thou that which is good in thine eyes.", insight:"'We are thy servants'; the house of Ahab surrendered without a sword drawn."},
{q:"What did Jehu's second letter require?", options:["Take the heads of your master's sons, and come to me to Jezreel by tomorrow","Bring the princes alive to Jezreel","Burn the palace of Ahab","Exile the royal family"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:6",verse:"Then he wrote a letter the second time to them, saying, If ye be mine, and if ye will hearken unto my voice, take ye the heads of the men your master’s sons, and come to me to Jezreel by to morrow this time. Now the king’s sons, being seventy persons, were with the great men of the city, which brought them up.", insight:"Heads in baskets by tomorrow; Jehu made cowards do the killing."},
{q:"What arrived at Jezreel the next day?", options:["The heads of the seventy sons in baskets","The seventy princes alive and bound","A chest of gold","A letter of surrender"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:7",verse:"And it came to pass, when the letter came to them, that they took the king’s sons, and slew seventy persons, and put their heads in baskets, and sent him them to Jezreel.", insight:"Seventy heads in baskets; the dynasty ended in a delivery."},
{q:"Where did Jehu lay the heads?", options:["In two heaps at the entering in of the gate until the morning","In the king's tomb","On the altar of Baal","In the river"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:8",verse:"And there came a messenger, and told him, saying, They have brought the heads of the king’s sons. And he said, Lay ye them in two heaps at the entering in of the gate until the morning.", insight:"Two heaps at the gate; judgment was displayed where all could see."},
{q:"What did Jehu tell the people in the morning?", options:["Ye be righteous: I conspired and slew my master, but who slew all these?","I am innocent of this blood","The LORD commanded me alone","Let no one speak of this"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:9",verse:"And it came to pass in the morning, that he went out, and stood, and said to all the people, Ye be righteous: behold, I conspired against my master, and slew him: but who slew all these?", insight:"'Who slew all these?' Jehu spread the guilt around; shared guilt is dodged guilt."},
{q:"What did Jehu declare about the word of the LORD?", options:["Nothing of the word of the LORD concerning the house of Ahab shall fall to the earth","The prophets were mistaken","Elijah's word is past","God has changed His mind"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:10",verse:"Know now that there shall fall unto the earth nothing of the word of the LORD, which the LORD spake concerning the house of Ahab: for the LORD hath done that which he spake by his servant Elijah.", insight:"Not one word falls; even Jehu knew God's sentence stands."},
{q:"Whom else did Jehu slay in Jezreel?", options:["All that remained of the house of Ahab, his great men, his kinsfolks, and his priests","Only the seventy princes","The worshippers of Baal","The elders of the city"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:11",verse:"So Jehu slew all that remained of the house of Ahab in Jezreel, and all his great men, and his kinsfolks, and his priests, until he left him none remaining.", insight:"Great men, kinsfolks, priests; judgment left Ahab no branch to regrow."},
{q:"Whom did Jehu meet at the shearing house?", options:["The brethren of Ahaziah king of Judah","The sons of the prophets","Hazael's ambassadors","The elders of Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:13",verse:"Jehu met with the brethren of Ahaziah king of Judah, and said, Who are ye? And they answered, We are the brethren of Ahaziah; and we go down to salute the children of the king and the children of the queen.", insight:"Forty-two men walking into the wrong place at the wrong time."},
{q:"How many of Ahaziah's brethren were slain?", options:["Two and forty men","Seventy","Thirty","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:14",verse:"And he said, Take them alive. And they took them alive, and slew them at the pit of the shearing house, even two and forty men; neither left he any of them.", insight:"Two and forty; Judah's royal visitors paid for Ahab's alliance."},
{q:"Whom did Jehu meet on the road to Samaria?", options:["Jehonadab the son of Rechab","Elisha the prophet","The king of Judah","A company of Levites"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:15",verse:"And when he was departed thence, he lighted on Jehonadab the son of Rechab coming to meet him: and he saluted him, and said to him, Is thine heart right, as my heart is with thy heart? And Jehonadab answered, It is. If it be, give me thine hand. And he gave him his hand; and he took him up to him into the chariot.", insight:"Jehonadab, a righteous outsider; God gives zealous men honest witnesses."},
{q:"What did Jehu ask Jehonadab?", options:["Is thine heart right, as my heart is with thy heart?","Wilt thou serve Baal with me?","Where are Ahab's sons?","Wilt thou be my captain?"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:15",verse:"And when he was departed thence, he lighted on Jehonadab the son of Rechab coming to meet him: and he saluted him, and said to him, Is thine heart right, as my heart is with thy heart? And Jehonadab answered, It is. If it be, give me thine hand. And he gave him his hand; and he took him up to him into the chariot.", insight:"'Is thine heart right?' Zeal seeks company before it seeks counsel."},
{q:"What did Jehu invite Jehonadab to witness?", options:["Come with me, and see my zeal for the LORD","The crowning of a new king","The building of a temple","The destruction of Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:16",verse:"And he said, Come with me, and see my zeal for the LORD. So they made him ride in his chariot.", insight:"'See my zeal'; advertised zeal should make us watch the ending."},
{q:"What did Jehu tell the people about serving Baal?", options:["Ahab served Baal a little; but Jehu shall serve him much","Baal is a false god, let us destroy him","I will serve Baal all my days","Baal has blessed Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:18",verse:"And Jehu gathered all the people together, and said unto them, Ahab served Baal a little; but Jehu shall serve him much.", insight:"A lie for a holy war; Jehu used deception as his weapon."},
{q:"Whom did Jehu summon to the solemn assembly?", options:["All the prophets of Baal, all his servants, and all his priests","The elders of Israel","The Levites","The captains of the army"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:19",verse:"Now therefore call unto me all the prophets of Baal, all his servants, and all his priests; let none be wanting: for I have a great sacrifice to do to Baal; whosoever shall be wanting, he shall not live. But Jehu did it in subtilty, to the intent that he might destroy the worshippers of Baal.", insight:"Every Baal worshipper in Israel gathered; the trap was set with their own devotion."},
{q:"What became of the house of Baal?", options:["They brake it down and made it a draught house unto this day","It became a temple to the LORD","It was burned with fire from heaven","It was turned into a palace"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:27",verse:"And they brake down the image of Baal, and brake down the house of Baal, and made it a draught house unto this day.", insight:"A draught house, a latrine; idolatry's grandest temple ended as a toilet."},
{q:"From what did Jehu not depart?", options:["The sins of Jeroboam, the golden calves in Bethel and in Dan","The worship of Baal","The high places of Judah","The counsel of Jehonadab"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 10:29",verse:"Howbeit from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin, Jehu departed not from after them, to wit, the golden calves that were in Bethel, and that were in Dan.", insight:"He destroyed Baal but kept the calves; partial obedience is polished disobedience."}
]}
]);
